00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:47,520
Oh, your jacket, it says
Corazon, are you mocking me?

265
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:52,100
And the heart pirates,
you think I didn't notice?

266
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:54,302
What are you trying to say here?

267
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:58,440
You refuse to accept the heart seat.

268
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,309
Then you bear the mark
of the heart anyway.

269
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:03,300
Why?

270
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,260
How insufferable.

271
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:24,460
Law, Corazon, that's enough.

272
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,960
This ends here.

273
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:31,320
Your crusade is dead and gone.

274
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:39,520
I'm finally free of this burden.

275
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:40,860
I'm free!

276
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,080
He can't proceed.

277
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:57,849
He has taken down Bellamy.

278
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,510
Well done.

279
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,277
Now there are only two
higher-ups left remaining.

280
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,740
Keep strong, Straw Hat.

281
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:08,440
He's making great strides. However,

282
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:13,780
the final obstacles awaiting him are
trouble, and, of course, Doflamingo himself.

283
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:19,210
No!

284
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:21,270
Viola!

285
00:21:21,353 --> 00:21:22,183
Something wrong?

286
00:21:26,980 --> 00:21:27,810
Viola?

287
00:21:27,893 --> 00:21:29,460
I have terrible news.

288
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:31,000
We're down a man too.

289
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:34,320
What's that mean?

290
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:35,914
Is someone in trouble?

291
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,340
It's Trafalgar Law.

292
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:05,320
King Rick?

293
00:22:05,540 --> 00:22:09,540
Despite our victories, the kingdom
is in great danger. Let's go.

294
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:12,060
Citizens may still require our aid.

295
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:13,600
We can't rest yet.

296
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:15,560
Sir, I'm coming.

297
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:19,920
Uh, me too! I'm joining
you. Count me in. Me too!

298
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:21,310
Very well.

299
00:22:21,660 --> 00:22:22,857
Let us descend into town.

300
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:26,840
It is not too late to minimize
the casualties further true.

301
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:29,528
Even if we can't fight
we can still help out

302
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:38,960
So what's the next step.

303
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:47,900
Let's wrap this up, sound good? Trouble!

304
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:56,030
TOPLAMENKO!

305
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:08,900
Took you long enough, Straw Hat.

306
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:11,280
How's dear old Bellamy doing?

307
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:16,357
Now that he has his freedom...

308
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:17,580
Don't play dumb!

309
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,340
You set this all up!

310
00:23:26,460 --> 00:23:28,757
You knew he'd never run away.

311
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,380
Come, come.

312
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:32,820
Come, come.

313
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:36,580
Spiderweb spread out.

314
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:41,810
Interesting.

315
00:23:41,893 --> 00:23:45,160
So I guess Bellamy didn't
hightail it after all?

316
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:48,880
What's so funny?

317
00:23:54,740 --> 00:23:56,480
Now come, come!

318
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:59,820
Hulk got my gun!

319
00:24:17,940 --> 00:24:19,780
And now, break white!

320
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:37,320
Hey, Traffy!

321
00:24:37,640 --> 00:24:39,699
Where's all this blood coming from?

322
00:24:39,940 --> 00:24:41,380
Where'd your arm go?

323
00:24:43,060 --> 00:24:44,817
Hey, Traffy! Hang in there!

324
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,720
Hey, Traffy!

325
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:54,220
What you can't tell—he's dead. Liar!

326
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:58,117
Just look at him.

327
00:24:58,200 --> 00:25:00,757
Trafi was holding out
for you to come through.

328
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:01,917
What a damn shame!

329
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:02,830
He

330
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:09,397
did mention that you're quite
the miracle worker, Straw Hat.

331
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:10,310
I

332
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:12,290
don't know.

333
00:25:12,373 --> 00:25:14,717
You didn't impress me
much in our first fight.

334
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:15,630
fight

335
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:19,657
And I doubt you stand a
chance against both of us.

336
00:25:19,740 --> 00:25:21,740
You'll pay for this, you bastards!

337
00:25:38,300 --> 00:25:39,130
Wait!

338
00:25:39,300 --> 00:25:40,476
Hold your positions!

339
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:53,720
Oh, no!

340
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:54,920
Let's back up!

341
00:25:59,160 --> 00:26:00,240
That's shrinking!

342
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:09,940
You'll be joining your
pal, Law, in no time.

343
00:26:13,060 --> 00:26:14,337
And now...

344
00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:17,140
We end this game. Mingo!

345
00:26:18,260 --> 00:26:19,380
Wait.

346
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:23,380
Listen carefully, Straw Hat.

347
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:35,440
Oh no!

348
00:26:50,100 --> 00:26:51,800
It's moving! I knew it!

349
00:26:56,940 --> 00:26:58,320
Those killer strings!

350
00:26:58,580 --> 00:26:59,577
They're closing ends!

351
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:00,490
Run away!

352
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,860
The end of the town isn't safer anymore!

353
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:19,120
Go, go, go!

354
00:27:22,660 --> 00:27:24,320
Say thank you in the west!

355
00:27:26,460 --> 00:27:28,401
Reporting from Carta in the east.

356
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:31,340
The birdcage is moving,
as the report said.

357
00:27:37,900 --> 00:27:40,429
Everyone is fleeing to
downtown in a panic!

358
00:27:42,620 --> 00:27:44,360
No one will survive.

359
00:27:45,760 --> 00:27:48,172
They'll all be butchered sooner or later.

360
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,120
Oh, I'm sorry.

361
00:27:53,460 --> 00:27:54,960
The rules have changed.

362
00:27:55,260 --> 00:27:57,820
I've decided to play a different game now.

363
00:27:58,080 --> 00:28:00,021
You're still calling this a game?

364
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:05,200
Just listen.

365
00:28:06,860 --> 00:28:10,840
The birdcage that surrounds
the kingdom started shrinking,

366
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:13,360
pulling into the center bit by bit.

367
00:28:15,620 --> 00:28:19,640
Think of it like a giant
umbrella closing slowly.

368
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:26,620
It'll cut through everything in
its path, the entire kingdom.

369
00:28:27,220 --> 00:28:32,480
As for how long that'll take,
well, about an hour, I'd say.

370
00:28:37,540 --> 00:28:41,140
They have nowhere left
to go; they're finished.

371
00:28:42,740 --> 00:28:46,457
Check for citizens at the edge of the
kingdom and bring them to the center quickly,

372
00:28:46,540 --> 00:28:47,440
yes sir!

373
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:55,957
We've moved the people at risk
from the edges of the kingdom,

374
00:28:56,040 --> 00:28:57,569
but we have to keep going.

375
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:59,060
Let's go!

376
00:28:59,260 --> 00:29:00,340
Follow after me!

377
00:29:00,520 --> 00:29:01,697
The strings are coming!

378
00:29:01,780 --> 00:29:02,610
Hurry!

379
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:06,220
Hey, could somebody untie us, please?

380
00:29:06,580 --> 00:29:08,300
Just the feet is fine, okay?

381
00:29:08,980 --> 00:29:09,880
Have mercy!

382
00:29:10,220 --> 00:29:11,540
I don't want to die!

383
00:29:12,740 --> 00:29:13,570
What?

384
00:29:13,653 --> 00:29:15,600
The birdcage is freaking? No!

385
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:19,337
Hey, birdcage, stop it!

386
00:29:19,420 --> 00:29:20,479
It seems to be so.

387
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:21,470
Come on, really?

388
00:29:21,553 --> 00:29:22,580
What should we do?

389
00:29:22,740 --> 00:29:24,520
We've suffered enough already!

390
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:25,817
Zoro, help!

391
00:29:25,900 --> 00:29:28,480
And we were winning
all of our fights, too!

392
00:29:28,640 --> 00:29:31,287
You can't pull the rug
out from under us now!

393
00:29:32,380 --> 00:29:33,210
Huh?

394
00:29:33,860 --> 00:29:36,977
We finally made it out of that
dungeon after all this time?

395
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:38,740
And now we're in a new cage?

396
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,586
There has to be some
place safe we can run to!

397
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:44,257
How could you do such a heartless thing?

398
00:29:44,340 --> 00:29:47,164
Is there no depth you
won't sink to, Doflamingo?

399
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:51,065
The birdcage is going to dice up
the whole kingdom at this rate!

400
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:52,660
We're all done for!

401
00:29:52,900 --> 00:29:53,760
Our home, too!

402
00:29:58,440 --> 00:30:01,717
I'm seeing a lot of smoke and
hearing a lot of rumbling.

403
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,447
There's no way this is good.

404
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,360
Hurry it up, Luffy!

405
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:08,660
Just kick his ass and
get this mess over with!

406
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:10,940
You're our only hope! Indeed!

407
00:30:11,220 --> 00:30:12,985
Thwart him swiftly, my friend!

408
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:17,520
It must be difficult to have so
much resting on one man's shoulders.

409
00:30:19,580 --> 00:30:20,560
Sir Luffy!

410
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:22,580
Please prevail!

411
00:30:23,260 --> 00:30:25,613
Everyone will die if you do not succeed!

412
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:35,680
I won't spare a single
rotten life in this kingdom.

413
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:42,920
They aren't worth a thing to me.

414
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:47,692
Not since they discovered the truth
about how I've been running this place.

415
00:30:54,860 --> 00:30:59,117
Every building, every
person, every animal,

416
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:02,357
all your miserable little allies,

417
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:07,160
and finally you will die.

418
00:31:16,660 --> 00:31:19,977
Although I suppose some of
your friends have died already,

419
00:31:20,060 --> 00:31:21,377
the good doctor passed away.

420
00:31:21,460 --> 00:31:22,580
just a moment ago.

421
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:29,400
So much for your pirate
alliance with dear old Traffy.

422
00:31:36,760 --> 00:31:39,657
Oh, but no need to worry about me.

423
00:31:39,740 --> 00:31:41,840
I'll build a new kingdom.

424
00:31:42,700 --> 00:31:43,877
Yeah, screw that.

425
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:46,937
All I gotta do is kick your ass
and everything will be fine.

426
00:31:47,020 --> 00:31:51,037
I'm starting to think that you're not
paying attention to me, Straw Hat?

427
00:31:51,120 --> 00:31:52,860
You'll never learn, do you?

428
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:54,100
Bullet strip

429
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:59,740
I'm gone Go ahead.

430
00:32:00,060 --> 00:32:01,700
You'll die just like Loh.

431
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:03,820
Shambles.

432
00:32:10,800 --> 00:32:14,260
Sorry, but nobody's dying here except you.

433
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,230
Go!

434
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:29,640
This operation will destroy
your body from the inside out.

435
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:35,620
Give a knife!

436
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:57,826
You were supposed to be
dead, you big cheater!

437
00:32:58,100 --> 00:33:02,000
And how can you do an app-a-tag
without making a room? I did.

438
00:33:02,220 --> 00:33:03,880
We're in a room as we speak.

439
00:33:05,260 --> 00:33:07,837
It'll shave some time
off my life, I'm sure.

440
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:11,920
But I made a room so big that you
can't see the end of it from here.

441
00:33:12,560 --> 00:33:13,390
What?

442
00:33:13,473 --> 00:33:14,303
But that's crazy!

443
00:33:16,840 --> 00:33:20,860
All I did was in
preparation for this moment!

444
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:42,720
It wasn't enough to kill me.

445
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:44,430
Shambles!

446
00:33:55,040 --> 00:33:55,870
Mingo!

447
00:33:57,040 --> 00:33:57,870
Wait.

448
00:34:00,620 --> 00:34:01,720
I'm alive.

449
00:34:04,060 --> 00:34:05,920
Listen carefully, Straw Hat.

450
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:08,200
Don't turn around.

451
00:34:08,580 --> 00:34:09,500
I have a plan.

452
00:34:13,220 --> 00:34:15,640
You can't defend against an attack.

453
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:16,800
I'm inside!

454
00:34:19,780 --> 00:34:22,480
Even you can counteract this technique.

455
00:34:39,740 --> 00:34:40,570
Doofy!

456
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:41,940
You're a king!

457
00:34:42,220 --> 00:34:44,700
A king never fought to his knees!

458
00:34:49,680 --> 00:34:51,720
You little bastard.

459
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:54,300
It's no use.

460
00:34:54,560 --> 00:34:56,840
Even if you kill me, you're done for.

461
00:35:01,820 --> 00:35:05,000
You think I won't kill you anyway?

462
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:10,900
You forget about me?

463
00:35:12,620 --> 00:35:14,620
I've got a gun, Chester!

464
00:35:20,460 --> 00:35:21,720
Oh, no!

465
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:29,400
Dolphi!

466
00:35:29,860 --> 00:35:30,800
Are you okay?

467
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:37,160
What more? Straw Hat. Hold on.

468
00:35:44,720 --> 00:35:50,820
Traffy It has to be.

469
00:35:52,100 --> 00:35:54,160
Me who does this!

470
00:36:28,620 --> 00:36:31,120
It's over, Doflamingo.

471
00:36:35,040 --> 00:36:36,880
What have you done?

472
00:36:37,160 --> 00:36:38,100
You're me!

473
00:36:38,360 --> 00:36:39,760
How dare you!

474
00:36:49,120 --> 00:36:50,620
Don't get in our way!

475
00:37:01,860 --> 00:37:02,897
Your family...

476
00:37:02,980 --> 00:37:05,977
is nothing more than people
you thought you could use.

477
00:37:06,060 --> 00:37:10,060
A bond built entirely on
your own ego and convenience.

478
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:13,297
And your only true brother.

479
00:37:13,380 --> 00:37:15,977
Who tried to stop you on
your path to destruction?

480
00:37:16,060 --> 00:37:18,160
Was murdered by you.

481
00:37:19,780 --> 00:37:22,320
Cause Lost finally, free now!

482
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:34,897
Yeah, I know.

483
00:37:34,980 --> 00:37:36,660
That was unfortunate.

484
00:37:38,100 --> 00:37:40,159
But he was the one who betrayed me.

485
00:37:40,740 --> 00:37:42,697
He was the one who pointed a gun.

486
00:37:42,780 --> 00:37:44,537
You think I wanted that?

487
00:37:44,620 --> 00:37:46,032
Don't give me that crap!

488
00:37:46,900 --> 00:37:49,782
You knew damn well he
wouldn't pull that trigger.

489
00:37:55,600 --> 00:37:57,720
I could have pulled it just fine.

490
00:38:05,620 --> 00:38:07,060
I bet so.

491
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:15,340
I always knew we were the same.

492
00:38:16,220 --> 00:38:18,820
I want to destroy everything that I see.

493
00:38:20,300 --> 00:38:22,220
People, towns.

494
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:25,346
I want to burn this whole
world to the ground.

495
00:38:27,780 --> 00:38:28,940
Maybe so.

496
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:32,260
But in this case, that's fine.

497
00:38:34,340 --> 00:38:36,020
Cause, I'll tell you this.

498
00:38:41,400 --> 00:38:44,165
You were the one who
should have died that day.

499
00:38:46,160 --> 00:38:49,537
If you're expecting me to say
something cold and twisted?

500
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:51,040
Then I'll indulge you.

501
00:38:53,340 --> 00:38:55,080
I hated Corazon.

502
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:58,617
He was a nuisance and an obstacle to me.

503
00:38:58,700 --> 00:39:01,377
His insipid sense of justice.

504
00:39:01,460 --> 00:39:04,620
This is worthless
sentimentality holding me back.

505
00:39:04,840 --> 00:39:06,440
He wasn't worth a damn.

506
00:39:06,840 --> 00:39:10,840
And that's why, when I killed
him that day, I was happy.

507
00:39:11,340 --> 00:39:12,440
Go to shock!

508
00:39:16,340 --> 00:39:17,900
You go to hell!

509
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:19,400
I've heard enough!

510
00:39:22,600 --> 00:39:23,520
Help me!

511
00:39:42,980 --> 00:39:45,400
Oh, my God.

512
00:40:15,680 --> 00:40:17,400
That's our cake for ya!

513
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:19,880
Can't keep a straight man down!

514
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:25,820
What did you do?

515
00:40:29,740 --> 00:40:35,060
if i have enough time i can use my
powers to perform an operation of my own

516
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:39,177
right now beneath the skin my strings are

517
00:40:39,260 --> 00:40:42,277
reconstructing the organs
you so rudely damaged

518
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:46,797
what the hell just takes
creativity although

519
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:48,917
i don't know if i would
call this It's healing,

520
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:49,830
exactly.

521
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,751
You threw your life away.

522
00:40:58,320 --> 00:41:00,500
Sticky, sticky cheese!

523
00:41:03,280 --> 00:41:04,480
Let me go!

524
00:41:06,040 --> 00:41:07,840
Stick sticker!

525
00:41:19,240 --> 00:41:20,240
And look at that.

526
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:22,146
I still get to do the honors.

527
00:41:29,680 --> 00:41:30,560
Damn it!

528
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:38,320
Damn it.

529
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:49,120
Thank you.
